On Nov 29, 6:10=A0am, BanMido <smartrefere...@gmail.com> wrote:
> I have an empty marker which was used up for enchanting my armor. So I
> should use the second one for recharging the marker, yes?

If you have the paper and marker charges, an uncursed charging scroll
is just as efficient as a blessed one on an empty magic marker (and
markers are best emptied before charging), but if your wish gives you
the two scrolls and you've no other source of charging I'd say using
the second on the marker makes sense.

Another thing is to make sure your luck is positive before you start
wishing at all, but it's very likely to be unless you've been playing
very strangely.  You can check with a wand or potion of enlightenment,
but it's probably safe to assume that you don't need to in this game.

> Right, so SDSM is at its limit with +4, correct? The wiki says T-
> shirts can be enchanted upto +5, so an uncursed scroll of enchant
> armor would do, wouldn't it?

All armor can be safely enchanted when it's at +3.  Blessed scrolls
might take that to +4 or to +5, but if it's already at +4 it's NOT
safe to try and enchant it to +5 (you'd have to get it back to +3
first - this is usually not worth doing).

Elven armor (helms, boots and cloaks) and all weapons can safely be
enchanted when they're at +5.  Blessed scrolls might take that to +6
or +7, same rule as above about enchanting +6 stuff applies.

